# Household

> Status: Ready
> Priority: P0
> Depends On: Authentication
> Next Feature: Account

---

# Overview

Household is the root entity for all financial data in Kin Finance.

Every financial data must belong to exactly one Household. A Household can be used by one person (personal) or many members (family).

In MVP, each user only has one Household.

---

# Goals

- Provide a root for all financial data.
- Connect all features to Household.
- Make the first user the Owner.
- Foundation for the permission system.

---

# Scope

## In Scope

- Create the first Household.
- Get active Household.
- Rename Household.

## Out of Scope

- Multiple Households.
- Household Switching.
- Household Archive.
- Household Delete.
- Invite Member.
- Transfer Ownership.

---

# User Stories

### Create Household

As a new user,

I want to create my first Household,

So that I can start using Kin Finance.

---

### Rename Household

As an Owner,

I want to change my Household name,

So that the Household name fits my needs.

